  "an4.53:11.4": "<i>Sama,</i> which means, “even,” “equal,” “on pitch,” or “in tune.” Throughout ancient cultures, the terminology of music was used to describe the moral quality of people and acts. Discordant intervals or poorly-tuned musical instruments were metaphors for evil; harmonious intervals and well-tuned instruments, for good. See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.55'>AN 4:55</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.16'>AN 6:16</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp235-255#dhp246'>Dhp 246–248</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp306-319#dhp309'>Dhp 309–310</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp2.14'>Sn 2:14</a>",
